# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_plan_event_ordering.py" "PLAN-EVENT ORDERING GATE: PASS" "plan-event ordering" "plan-event ordering (audit iter-5 P2: the marketplace/billing plan setter is now MONOTONIC against UNORDERED, RE-DELIVERABLE webhooks -- a re-delivered cancelled->free arriving AFTER a later purchased->pro is REFUSED, so a paying customer is not wrongly throttled; the LATER event still wins on the ordered path; an equal/newer event applies; a NULL effective_at is inert [value-idempotency unchanged, plants no barrier]; tenant-scoped; both uninstall purge + GDPR erase forget the per-account high-water mark; the mark lives in a NEW FK-free core.account_plan_event table [contention-free prod apply, REVOKEd from PUBLIC] -- LIVE-PATH billing change)" "plan-event ordering / billing monotonicity (set_account_plan_with_authority refuses a STRICTLY-older marketplace event via a per-account effective_date high-water mark in a new FK-free core.account_plan_event; mirrors the graph-ingest captured_at guard; SECURITY/BILLING-sensitive -- it governs the paid quota wall)" 30
